1
00:00:00,440 --> 00:00:06,880
Three Civilizations: G.D.P. Trajectories Earth grows at two point five percent.

2
00:00:07,760 --> 00:00:13,950
Wishonia redirects its bomb budget, cures diseases, and fixes its governance.

3
00:00:14,200 --> 00:00:19,140
Moronia keeps building weapons until G.D.P. hits zero dollars.

4
00:00:19,760 --> 00:00:25,060
The expected value math is not subtle. Your species has three options.

5
00:00:25,720 --> 00:00:32,280
You can keep doing what you're doing, which your economists optimistically project at two point five percent annual growth.

6
00:00:33,060 --> 00:00:40,280
You can redirect your weapons budget into medical research, fix your broken governance, and compound your way to a civilization

7
00:00:40,280 --> 00:00:48,940
that would be unrecognizable to you. Or you can accelerate your arms race until someone's automated defense system makes

8
00:00:48,940 --> 00:00:54,620
a decision that can't be undone, which produces a growth rate of negative everything.

9
00:00:55,500 --> 00:00:59,760
I modeled all three over twenty years. Within most of your lifetimes.

10
00:00:59,960 --> 00:01:08,220
Three Futures. Earth: The Baseline Nobody Questions. Earth continues at two point five percent annual G.D.P.

11
00:01:08,520 --> 00:01:14,420
growth. By year twenty, global G.D.P. reaches roughly one hundred and eighty-eight trillion dollars.

12
00:01:14,700 --> 00:01:23,320
Not bad. But not what happens when you actually focus. This baseline assumes no major wars, no pandemics worse than COVID,

13
00:01:23,800 --> 00:01:27,600
no catastrophes. The best-case version of your current trajectory.

14
00:01:28,520 --> 00:01:33,860
We're being generous. Wishonia: What Happens When You Stop Wasting Money.

15
00:01:34,680 --> 00:01:42,040
There are two versions of this path. The Treaty Path is just the one percent treaty: move murder money to medicine money,

16
00:01:42,180 --> 00:01:50,780
cure diseases, let the savings compound. The Wishonia Path is what happened on my planet: we liked the treaty so much we

17
00:01:50,780 --> 00:01:54,920
pointed incentive alignment bonds at everything else that was broken too.

18
00:01:55,780 --> 00:02:01,650
The peace dividend chapter showed the direct savings. Here's what happens when those savings compound.

19
00:02:02,840 --> 00:02:06,500
(A.I. is excluded from this model because it helps everybody equally.

20
00:02:06,900 --> 00:02:11,610
The difference between these paths is purely about where you point your money and your engineers.).

21
00:02:12,280 --> 00:02:16,200
You stop pointing engineers at missiles and point them at medicine.

22
00:02:16,580 --> 00:02:24,860
G.D.P. grows faster. When your species did this after World War Two, you cut military spending by eighty-seven percent in

23
00:02:24,860 --> 00:02:30,400
two years (nineteen forty-five to nineteen forty-seven, from forty percent of G.D.P.

24
00:02:30,500 --> 00:02:35,560
to three point five percent) and got the biggest economic boom in your history.

25
00:02:36,380 --> 00:02:43,740
The Wishonia model is more conservative: a three-year transition ramp to eighty-seven point six percent reallocation.

26
00:02:44,400 --> 00:02:49,320
Military research accidentally gave you the internet, G.P.S., and jet engines.

27
00:02:50,060 --> 00:02:55,260
Medical research has already accidentally given you CRISPR, messenger R.N.A.

28
00:02:55,400 --> 00:03:02,350
(or M.R.N.A.) platforms, and A.I. protein folding. Imagine what happens when you do it on purpose.

29
00:03:03,140 --> 00:03:08,160
The research spillover multiplier (two times) is from your own published studies.

30
00:03:08,880 --> 00:03:18,060
People stop being sick. Disease currently costs your civilization thirteen percent of G.D.P.: five trillion dollars in people

31
00:03:18,300 --> 00:03:23,580
too sick to work plus nine point nine trillion dollars in trying to fix them.

32
00:03:23,820 --> 00:03:27,560
You currently produce first treatments for about fifteen diseases per year.

33
00:03:28,180 --> 00:03:35,420
Your decentralized F.D.A., scaled to the physical ceiling of how many humans can participate in trials (five hundred and

34
00:03:35,800 --> 00:03:43,660
sixty-six times), clears one hundred percent of the six thousand six hundred and fifty diseases you currently have no treatment

35
00:03:43,660 --> 00:03:49,480
for. As diseases get cured, all that lost productivity comes back as growth.

36
00:03:50,300 --> 00:03:57,960
Your governments stop losing money to stupidity. The political dysfunction tax documents one hundred and one trillion dollars

37
00:03:57,960 --> 00:04:06,640
per year in money your governments waste on corruption, redundancy, regulations written before computers existed, and nine

38
00:04:06,640 --> 00:04:15,340
agencies doing the same thing. On Wishonia, we used incentive alignment bonds to pay people for fixing these problems instead

39
00:04:15,340 --> 00:04:23,820
of perpetuating them. Turns out that works. The recovered money goes to whatever produces the most value: migration reform,

40
00:04:24,000 --> 00:04:27,760
lead elimination, science funding, regulatory modernization.

41
00:04:28,460 --> 00:04:35,440
These four things compound on each other. Better-funded research produces innovations, which cure diseases, which make people

42
00:04:35,500 --> 00:04:39,540
healthier and more productive, which increases the return on everything else.

43
00:04:40,120 --> 00:04:44,700
It's a virtuous cycle. You're currently running the vicious version of it.

44
00:04:45,620 --> 00:04:53,140
By year twenty, the two paths separate dramatically. The Treaty Path (just the murder-money-to-medicine-money part) grows

45
00:04:53,140 --> 00:05:01,660
at seventeen point nine percent per year and reaches three point one one quadrillion dollars, which is sixteen point five

46
00:05:01,660 --> 00:05:10,380
times Earth's baseline. The Wishonia Path (treaty plus fixing the dysfunction tax) grows at twenty-five point four percent

47
00:05:10,380 --> 00:05:17,020
per year and reaches ten point seven quadrillion dollars, which is fifty-six point seven times Earth's baseline.

48
00:05:17,940 --> 00:05:25,540
The Wishonia Path is three point four three times the Treaty Path, because fixing your governance multiplies everything

49
00:05:25,540 --> 00:05:32,700
else. Moronia: The Arithmetic of Extinction. Moronia is what happens when you do the opposite.

50
00:05:33,340 --> 00:05:40,540
Instead of redirecting military spending, you increase it. Arms races escalate, and eventually someone's automated defense

51
00:05:40,540 --> 00:05:46,860
system makes a decision that can't be undone. From years zero to five: Business as usual.

52
00:05:47,300 --> 00:05:51,750
Two point five percent growth. Everyone insists the arms race is "stabilizing."

53
00:05:52,420 --> 00:05:56,460
Experts write papers about "strategic equilibrium." The papers are well-cited.

54
00:05:57,340 --> 00:06:03,320
From years five to ten: Infrastructure stress, trade disruptions, and proxy wars intensify.

55
00:06:04,140 --> 00:06:10,960
Growth declines to negative five percent. From years ten to fifteen: Supply chains collapse, institutions lose legitimacy,

56
00:06:10,960 --> 00:06:10,960
and regional conflicts merge. G.D.P. falls at negative five to negative fifteen percent annually.

57
00:06:10,960 --> 00:06:15,600
From years fifteen to twenty: Terminal decline. G.D.P. reaches zero at year twenty.

58
00:06:16,300 --> 00:06:21,480
Moronia's G.D.P. at year twenty is zero dollars. This is not a rounding error.

59
00:06:21,940 --> 00:06:26,840
This is the number you get when you multiply any positive number by zero surviving humans.

60
00:06:27,960 --> 00:06:32,380
The Expected Value. "But what if the treaty doesn't work as well as you claim?"

61
00:06:33,100 --> 00:06:39,780
Fine. Give the Wishonia Path a ninety percent chance of working and a ten percent chance of total extinction.

62
00:06:40,620 --> 00:06:48,040
Multiply the Wishonia Path G.D.P. of ten point seven quadrillion dollars by its probability, and you get an expected value

63
00:06:48,040 --> 00:06:55,720
of nine point six two quadrillion dollars. The extinction path contributes zero dollars, because there's nobody left to

64
00:06:55,720 --> 00:07:01,060
have a G.D.P. That expected value is fifty-one times the status quo.

65
00:07:01,560 --> 00:07:06,580
Even after accounting for the possibility that it all goes wrong, you're still better off trying.

66
00:07:07,140 --> 00:07:12,160
This is not a close call. What This Means Per Person. G.D.P.

67
00:07:12,200 --> 00:07:15,880
in the trillions is abstract. Here's what it means for actual humans.

68
00:07:16,820 --> 00:07:22,420
If Earth stays on its current path, average income by year twenty is twenty thousand five hundred dollars.

69
00:07:22,680 --> 00:07:28,800
That's roughly where Poland is today. The Treaty Path gets you to three hundred and thirty-nine thousand dollars.

70
00:07:29,640 --> 00:07:33,060
The Wishonia Path gets you to one point one six million dollars.

71
00:07:34,140 --> 00:07:41,280
These are G.D.P. per capita using U.N. population projections of nine point two billion of people for twenty forty-five.

72
00:07:42,060 --> 00:07:48,620
Average, not median, because we make no assumptions about distribution (though a civilization that has fixed its governance

73
00:07:48,620 --> 00:07:56,980
probably also has less inequality). The Wishonia numbers look implausible only if you've never seen a graph of G.D.P.

74
00:07:57,020 --> 00:08:00,120
before and after your Industrial Revolution. You've done this before.

75
00:08:00,760 --> 00:08:05,190
You just did it by accident last time. Go Ahead, Change the Numbers.

76
00:08:06,240 --> 00:08:10,100
Every input to this model is a named variable you can look up and argue with.

77
00:08:10,900 --> 00:08:17,500
The disease cure fraction (one hundred percent) comes from trial-capacity scaling with a physical participant ceiling.

78
00:08:17,920 --> 00:08:22,040
The research spillover multiplier (two x) comes from published studies.

79
00:08:22,500 --> 00:08:30,700
If any assumption is wrong, change it. The model still dwarfs Earth's baseline, because no plausible adjustment to any single

80
00:08:30,700 --> 00:08:37,179
number eliminates the effect of four compounding mechanisms running simultaneously for twenty years.

81
00:08:38,220 --> 00:08:42,100
The question is not "will the treaty produce exactly these returns?"

82
00:08:42,480 --> 00:08:48,800
The question is "does redirecting murder money to medicine money produce better results than not doing so?"

83
00:08:49,740 --> 00:08:54,360
The answer is yes under every scenario where you prefer being alive to being dead.

84
00:08:55,300 --> 00:09:01,380
The peace dividend gives you the annual numbers. The Wishonia model gives you the institutional design.

85
00:09:01,720 --> 00:09:08,640
The Moronia model gives you the counterfactual. The political dysfunction tax gives you the waste ledger.

86
00:09:09,040 --> 00:09:12,240
The incentive alignment bonds give you the mechanism that fixes it.

87
00:09:12,900 --> 00:09:16,740
This chapter gives you what happens when you run them all forward twenty years.
